    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for E.164 telephone numbers in the owner intake path.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\nThe `normalizeTelephone(...)` method already normalized submitted numbers to E.164 form and enforced the general \"`+` followed by 8\u201315 digits\" syntax. I added a country-code-aware length check on top of it:\n\n- A `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` map declares the required national-digit count per known country code: `+61` \u2192 9, `+1` \u2192 10.\n- A new `validateNationalNumberLength(...)` helper strips the `+`, finds the **longest** matching country code (so a shorter code can't shadow a longer one), and throws `InvalidFieldsException` (rendered as HTTP 400 naming `telephone`) when the digits after the code don't have the exact expected length. Unrecognized country codes fall back to the existing general 8\u201315 digit rule.\n\nThis is reached from both create (`prepareNewOwner` \u2192 `normalizeTelephone`) and update paths, so both are covered.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The new test `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (posts `+61 123`, expects 400) passes.\n- The generated valid telephone (`04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 9 national digits under `+61`) and existing flows remain valid, so the full suite stays green.",
